# Cloudflare Workers static-asset redirects (same format as _headers).
# Applies to both roc-lang.org and www.roc-lang.org, since both are served by
# the same Worker.
#
# These paths existed on the old website and are still linked from elsewhere
# (e.g. the READMEs in roc-lang/examples), so they must not 404. Until the
# migration to the new compiler these rules were generated by
# write_builtins_redirects! in build_website.roc; they are a plain file now
# because nothing in them is derived from the build any more.
#
# Two Cloudflare details drive the shape of these rules:
#
# 1. Rules without a splat/placeholder are "static" and are matched by exact
#    path lookup, ahead of every dynamic rule. There is no trailing-slash
#    fallback, so each static path needs both spellings spelled out.
# 2. Despite what the docs imply, file order is NOT honored between two dynamic
#    rules that both match a path. A catch-all `/builtins/*` placed last still
#    won over the earlier `/builtins/main/*`, which is what sent
#    /builtins/main/Str to the non-existent /docs/main/main/Str.
#
# So the dynamic rules below must not overlap each other. The version rules
# consume a version segment via a splat; un-versioned module links use a
# `:module` placeholder, which matches a single segment only (never across a
# `/`) and therefore cannot collide with them. The one remaining overlap --
# `/builtins/main/` matching both `/builtins/:module/` and `/builtins/main/*` --
# is settled by the static rule for that exact path.
#
# ci_scripts/check-redirects.sh verifies every rule here still works, and fails
# if a rule has no test case, so add one there when adding a rule here.

# --- Static rules (exact paths; these win over the dynamic rules below) ---

# The tutorial currently lives in the roc repo; 302 because it is expected to
# move back onto this site.
/tutorial https://github.com/roc-lang/roc/blob/main/docs/mini-tutorial-new-compiler.md 302

# The builtin docs moved from /builtins/<Module> to /docs/main/<Module>. Inspect
# is the exception: main no longer has a module of its own, and its contents
# moved into Str. The released versions still have their own Inspect module, so
# only the un-versioned spellings need this exception.
/builtins/Inspect /docs/main/Str/#inspect 301
/builtins/Inspect/ /docs/main/Str/#inspect 301

# The roots of the moved docs, per version.
/builtins /docs/main/ 301
/builtins/ /docs/main/ 301
/builtins/main /docs/main/ 301
/builtins/main/ /docs/main/ 301
/builtins/alpha3 /docs/alpha3/ 301
/builtins/alpha3/ /docs/alpha3/ 301
/builtins/alpha4 /docs/alpha4/ 301
/builtins/alpha4/ /docs/alpha4/ 301

# The platforms page moved into the language reference.
/platforms /docs/main/langref/platforms/ 301
/platforms/ /docs/main/langref/platforms/ 301

# --- Dynamic rules (must not overlap each other; see note 2 above) ---

# Version-prefixed URLs keep their version: /builtins/alpha4/Str is the alpha4
# docs, not main's.
/builtins/main/* /docs/main/:splat 301
/builtins/alpha3/* /docs/alpha3/:splat 301
/builtins/alpha4/* /docs/alpha4/:splat 301

# Everything else under /builtins is an un-versioned module link (e.g.
# /builtins/Dict, still used by some example READMEs) and resolves to main.
/builtins/:module /docs/main/:module 301
/builtins/:module/ /docs/main/:module/ 301
